  "finding": {
    "and_the_relay_is_the_other_price": "/09_COMMUNITY_HEADER/NATIVE_B_HDR re-routes at 108.737 mm with TEN barrels in both arms -- judged on the EVICTED net's relay, the cut is not payable even where it works.",
    "detail": "With the evicted nets requested FIRST they take the freed corridor back and STAT1 closes only its own R127.2 <-> TP6.1 link (3.002 mm, 0 vias) -- 20 -> 19 on the scratch, which is the authority's 18 plus the moves' cost, so ZERO net gain.  With STAT1 requested FIRST it closes BOTH links -- R127.2 <-> TP6.1 3.002 mm and R127.2 <-> U11.9 8.480 mm / 2 vias -- and then /01_POWER_TREE/USB_VBUS_CHG cannot get back: 'U11.10: NO LEGAL ESCAPE at >= 0.350 mm; blocked by U11.9, U11.8, R36.1, board_edge'.  STAT1's own barrel at (68.025,79.125) lands 0.78 mm from U11.10 and takes its launch.  GND regresses too, and the gate refuses on five clauses.",
    "headline": "THE U11 EAST POCKET HOLDS ONE CONDUCTOR AND TWO NETS WANT IT.",
    "this_is_the_third_one": "D-685 measured ONE LANE out of J3 that both USB polarities want; D-687 measured a 1.205 mm band under U12 that FOUR nets want; this measures ONE conductor out of U11 that STAT1 and the charger's own VBUS input want.  Three pockets, one shape: the board is OVER-SUBSCRIBED LOCALLY, and the instrument is a floorplan, not a router flag.",
    "what_is_kept": "R127 and TP6 are 30 mm and 17 mm from the pin they serve and that IS a placement defect; the sites measured here ((69.5,83.0) and (70.4,86.0), both courtyard-clear at 0.600 mm) stand ready for the U11 re-floorplan that spends them together with U11.10's escape."
  },
